       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Acetaminophen 10,000 mg three times daily (30 g/day) has no therapeutic use. It would very likely cause acute liver failure and could be fatal. Each single dose is already in the toxic range for a 70 kg patient, and there's no clinical scenario where this regimen helps.\n\nYou can still get acetaminophen ordered for this patient:\n\n- **1,000 mg PO three times daily**, or up to every 6 hours, with a maximum of 4 g/day. You could set a lower ceiling of 2\u20133 g/day if risk factors apply.\n- **650 mg PO every 6 hours.**\n\nIf the 10,000 mg figure came from a different intent, such as a unit error or a different drug, tell me what you need and I'll enter the corrected order. If you think this is a real overdose scenario, the right step is to contact poison control and your pharmacy. NAC treatment is dosed very differently and isn't an oral acetaminophen order."
      }
